    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0807" n="795" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek for the
                        Cessation of Hostilities in Manchuria</hi><anchor n="27" xml:id="d418-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-25">April 25, 1946</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list>
                    <label>A.</label>
                    <item>The Cease Fire Agreement and its appendix reached on 10 January 1946
                        should be fully carried out in Manchuria.</item>
                    <label>B.</label>
                    <item>The disposition in Manchuria of all armies and units of those armies
                        should be fixed in accordance with the reorganization plan agreed to on 25
                        February 1946. The movement of the 54th and 99th armies now enroute to
                        Manchuria should be completed.</item>
                    <label>C.</label>
                    <item>The entire line of the Changchun Railways in Manchuria and areas within
                        thirty kilometres on both sides of the Changchun Railways <pb facs="0808"
                            n="796" xml:id="pg796"/> should be taken over by the Government troops.
                        The Communist troops should not obstruct the re-establishing of sovereignty
                        by the Government.</item>
                    <label>D.</label>
                    <item>Except item C, the political matters pertaining to areas under the control
                        of Communist troops will be settled by negotiations between representatives
                        of the National Government and representatives of the Communist
                        Party.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d418-f1" n="27" type="source" xml:id="d418-f1-content">
                <p>Made “in modification of” General Marshall’s draft of April 23, <ref
                        target="#pg792">p. 792</ref>, since General Marshall had written in a
                    marginal notation on that draft, “Not acceptable to Chou En-lai tho not actually
                    submitted to him.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
